t spatial vision, very good leadership qualities. Concerns: regarded as a show\u2011off, not open to new ideas, unfriendly, eats unhealthily. Also earlier we had \"unfriendly; eats unhealthily\" from Agent 3. Also \"show\u2011off\" and \"not open to new ideas\" from our notes. So we need to evaluate: A's strengths are safety-critical, but concerns about crew cooperation (unfriendly, show\u2011off) and health (eats unhealthily) affect reliability. Also not open to new ideas may affect adaptability.\n\nWe need to argue whether B still best or A could be better. B has communication concerns (pretentious, nasty remarks, grumpy) but also strong reliability, stress handling, technical competence. A has strong safety skills but interpersonal and health concerns.\n\nWe can argue that B's communication issues are less severe than A's unfriendly and health concerns, and B's reliability and stress handling are proven. So we keep vote for B, but note that A's strengths are notable but concerns outweigh.\n\nWe also need to maybe ask for any additional info on A's crew cooperation or health impact, but we have the facts. Could ask other panel members for more specifics, but we can just argue.\n\nThus: \"I agree with Agent 3 that A has strong safety skills, but the unfriendly attitude and health issues raise reliability concerns, and his lack of openness to new ideas suggests limited adaptability. Compared to B, whose reliability and stress handling are solid, and whose communication issues are more about tone that can be mitigated, I still recommend B.\"\n\nWe must include METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate B\"."}
